                                                "example_id": "5137e3cc-0891-4436-a371-693925c6df38",
                                                "sense_id": "a6455878-13f0-3a11-a88e-14bbd393a07d",
                                                "text": "[O]bſerving [...] abundance of Matter floating in the Urine like Bran, with a great Number of Recrements like Cuttings of Hair, ſome above an Inch long, which Subſtances were found in all the Water that I made in above Twelve Months; for which I could get no Remedy: I was adviſed to drink Water, which in about half a Year did intirely free me from thoſe Symptoms, [...]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "650db77c-9ac8-4080-ac7f-75c443216c98",
                                                "sense_id": "a6455878-13f0-3a11-a88e-14bbd393a07d",
                                                "text": "Frommer spoke to me—mostly in English—about the challenges of creating an entirely alien language."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27141017-15ce-4b27-a0b4-1192cd35b7f5",
                                                "sense_id": "a6455878-13f0-3a11-a88e-14bbd393a07d",
                                                "text": "Unlike Ali G Indahouse, Baron Cohen’s failed attempt to bring his most famous character into an entirely fictional universe, Borat found the comic tension in placing his Kazakhstani buffoon in delicate social situations, like a rodeo where he supports the “War Of Terror” a bit too zealously."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9ec32ff-97ef-4b1c-8f53-4e5da000d1d4",
                                                "sense_id": "a6455878-13f0-3a11-a88e-14bbd393a07d",
                                                "text": "As we age, the major arteries of our bodies frequently become thickened with plaque, a fatty material with an oatmeal-like consistency that builds up along the inner lining of blood vessels. The reason plaque forms isn’t entirely known, but it seems to be related to high levels of cholesterol inducing an inflammatory response, which can also attract and trap more cellular debris over time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47e1aa0b-25ad-389d-9b2d-47fd2b667994",
                                        "entry_id": "4aa3e8fd-b2f6-3cfa-b6e9-d69dd5c2960e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To the exclusion of others; solely;"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1556d055-9759-4b7c-8fa4-a85683f8a85d",
                                                "sense_id": "47e1aa0b-25ad-389d-9b2d-47fd2b667994",
                                                "text": "I'm entirely to blame."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7a1b465e-f1ed-4881-8198-5fb188904391",
                                                "sense_id": "47e1aa0b-25ad-389d-9b2d-47fd2b667994",
                                                "text": "This part of the park is used entirely by the workers; everyone else will have to go to the other side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fbe40f7c-b289-4ea5-b7f6-9a9732baa694",
                        "source_entry_id": "57fd3d30-ff22-3c17-86f3-28b830d64b61",
                        "source_sense_id": "ed954b2f-6afe-3700-935f-6dadcdafc82c",
                        "target_lang_word": "wholly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wholly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "864699c7-a0c5-348e-b9fd-31978b90b396",
                                        "entry_id": "a43d21e0-162c-3cf5-b0d0-998708fc7a1e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Completely and entirely; to the fullest extent; (loosely, exaggeratedly) very; to a great extent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01d98284-d541-4ae7-a614-a215a8c8108c",
                                                "sense_id": "864699c7-a0c5-348e-b9fd-31978b90b396",
                                                "text": "Wholly, in my opinion, this is wrong."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f52e3888-ab58-4751-afd8-0736aff36e39",
                                                "sense_id": "864699c7-a0c5-348e-b9fd-31978b90b396",
                                                "text": "And Moses sware on that day, saying, Surely the land whereon thy feet haue troden, shall be thine inheritance, and thy childrens for euer, because thou hast wholly followed the Lord my God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5b3d300-3f30-499b-abf4-feb9aa8c3f00",
                                                "sense_id": "864699c7-a0c5-348e-b9fd-31978b90b396",
                                                "text": "Carried somehow, somewhither, for some reason, on these surging floods, were these travelers, of errand not wholly obvious to their fellows, yet of such sort as to call into query alike the nature of their errand and their own relations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02fbbb5b-eade-4bb3-8b8b-28338aaf5425",
                                                "sense_id": "864699c7-a0c5-348e-b9fd-31978b90b396",
                                                "text": "‘You ain't very strong, are you?’ said a neighbour with sympathetic intent, and ‘You don't have very good health, I expect?’ asked another. Mr Colville said, ‘He do look wholly pale, that's a fact.’ The word ‘wholly’ thus used puzzled me for some time. In Suffolk it is used for ‘very’ or ‘really’, and crops up in almost every sentence. But at first I thought Mr Colville was ascribing to me an air of sanctity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48bf96e8-91f1-489f-92b4-919603035b91",
                                                "sense_id": "864699c7-a0c5-348e-b9fd-31978b90b396",
                                                "text": "With the descent of the cold war, relations between the two countries (for this is, to all intents and purposes, what they became after the end of the war) were almost completely broken off, with whole families split for the ensuing decades, some for ever. This event and its after-effects, along with the war against the Japanese in the 1940s, was to cast a long shadow over the years ahead, and led to the creation of the wholly unprecedented worship of Kim Il-sung, and his elevation to almost God-like status. It was also to create the system in which his son was to occupy almost as impossibly elevated a position."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88246de6-8abb-4abf-b690-1151c0bb3ec8",
                                                "sense_id": "864699c7-a0c5-348e-b9fd-31978b90b396",
                                                "text": "The explosion rocked the Riteng Computer Accessory Co., a wholly owned subsidiary of Pegatron, in Shanghai’s Songjiang district."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7cd2bb8-dd74-356d-81e8-fae419ff733a",
                                        "entry_id": "a43d21e0-162c-3cf5-b0d0-998708fc7a1e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Exclusively and solely."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d106a5b8-9d6c-4257-bf98-77197bf7ecd8",
                                                "sense_id": "d7cd2bb8-dd74-356d-81e8-fae419ff733a",
                                                "text": "A creature wholly given to brawls and wine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "89359d84-2188-46e2-92bb-84ac42aa25dd",
